# ⭐⭐ THE INLINE ANSWER OPTIONS REFERENCE (#189) — a coverage determination driven by a CODED QUESTION.
//
// Deliberately GENERIC: no customer content, no real policy. Its job is to be the golden oracle for the
// inline `value from:` construct and the `in qualifying` predicate, so a change to either shows up as a
// reviewable diff in BOTH emit lanes.
//
// What it exercises, and why each piece is here:
//
//   · INLINE OPTIONS — the codes live on the question, written ONCE, in the concept's OWN CodeSystem. No
//     system URL appears anywhere in this file, and none appears in the `.cel` beside it either.
//   · THE `qualifying` / `not qualifying` MARKER — required because this concept IS the subject of an
//     `in qualifying` predicate. Adding a fourth option cannot compile until it says what it does.
//   · A "NONE OF THE LISTED …" OPTION — the reason a denial costs ONE answer instead of one per option. With
//     the options unanswered the criterion is UNKNOWN and the tree PAUSES; answering `none` makes it a
//     determinate FALSE. That is the whole point of the construct, and it is what the `.cel` proves.
//   · A PURE QUESTION (`Service Requested`) — a plain local boolean with nothing that can compute it, so an
//     unanswered run pauses at the gate rather than reaching the outer `otherwise`.
library "Coded Question Reference".

// The gate. A bare `code is` boolean: nothing derives it, so unanswered it is UNKNOWN — not false.
concept "Service Requested":
- shape is Scalar.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `service-requested`.

// ⭐ THE CODED QUESTION. `shape is Record` + `most recent this` means it publishes ONE record: the newest
// answer wins, so a later answer overrides an earlier one.
concept "Documented Symptom":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- code is `documented-symptom`.
- definition is most recent this.
- value from:
  - `functional-limitation` display is `Functional limitation affecting daily activity`, qualifying.
  - `persistent-pain` display is `Persistent pain despite conservative therapy`, qualifying.
  - `none-of-listed` display is `None of the listed symptoms is documented`, not qualifying.

// ⭐ THE PREDICATE. No `type is`: this is an ephemeral derivation — it publishes a computed boolean, emits no
// resource, and gets no case-feature StructureDefinition.
concept "Qualifying Symptom Documented":
- shape is Scalar.
- value type is boolean.
- definition is "Documented Symptom" in qualifying.

activity "certify.Met":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `APPROVED`.

activity "not-certify.Unmet":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `NOT APPROVED`.

decision "Coverage Determination":
first:
- when "Service Requested" then:
    first:
    - when "Qualifying Symptom Documented" then recommend activity "certify.Met".
    - otherwise then recommend activity "not-certify.Unmet".
    end.
- otherwise then recommend activity "not-certify.Unmet".
